rong hand.\n\nReason:\nI have a full house (Kings full of Tens), which is an extremely strong hand. My opponent has been passively calling all my bets, suggesting they have something decent but not premium. The river card (5 of Clubs) is unlikely to have helped them. I want to extract value while keeping the bet size callable. A bet of around 2000 chips represents a strong value bet that can get called by weaker Kings or other strong-but-losing hands, while not being so large that it only gets called by better hands.\n\nAnswer: 2000"}
